o with these two different  numbers  that's a great question brian listen the  prosecution is seeking the maximum under  the law but what the defense is saying  is that if you use these federal  sentencing guidelines that maximum  should be reduced to 17 and what they do  with the guidelines they look at two  factors they look at the offense level  and they look at the criminal history  and what the defense is arguing here is  yes this is the high offense but low  criminal history and the calculation  should be less than the 25 it should be  17 but the judge to answer your question  is probably going to ignore the federal  sentencing guidelines because they are  just that guidelines they are not  mandatory they're discretionary and i  think the judge is probably going to  throw the book at r kelly yeah and i  expect if he does that expect an appeal  by his defense as well  prosecutors also want kelly to be fined  50 to 250 000 so  where does that money go and what if he  can't pay  well you know as a public defender they  put on these surcharges and fines to to  deter and punish if he doesn't have the  money to pay then it goes into  collections and they can seize whatever  assets he has they can um forfeit put  liens on his properties and things like  that and usually they say that you know  the money goes to support court systems  support government operations police  sanitation infrastructure and it usually  also goes to victim support funds to  help victims of crimes to get over their  uh their damage from the criminal  activity yeah i kind of see especially  with a case like this with so many  sexual assault victims that money may be  earmarked more so for that than anything  else thank you both for that breakdown  though when we come back could  brangelina soon be headed to a jury  trial why brad pitt says ex-wife  angelina jolie made a move to  intentionally harm him by selling off  shares of their wine company  [Music]  welcome back academy award-winning  ac